<section id="abstract">
  <h2>Abstract</h2>
  <p> Abstract</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Introduction</h2>
  <p>This document defines the core schema for the Orchestration Architect (OA), focusing on the concepts of Object, Category, and Morphism, and their application in a mind map structure.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Core</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt><code>oa:Object</code></dt>
    <dd>An abstract entity foundational to the OA schema.</dd>

    <dt><code>oa:Category</code></dt>
    <dd>A structure consisting of objects and morphisms between them.</dd>

    <dt><code>oa:Morphism</code></dt>
    <dd>A directional relationship between objects in a category.</dd>
  </dl>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Example Graph Structure</h2>
  <pre><code>@prefix oa: &lt;urn:oa:ns#&gt; .

oa:ExampleCategory a oa:Category ;
    rdfs:label "Example Category" ;
    oa:hasObject oa:Node1, oa:Node2 ;
    oa:hasMorphism oa:Edge1 .

oa:Node1 a oa:Object ;
    rdfs:label "Node 1" .

oa:Node2 a oa:Object ;
    rdfs:label "Node 2" .

oa:Edge1 a oa:Morphism ;
    rdfs:label "Link from Node 1 to Node 2" ;
    oa:source oa:Node1 ;
    oa:target oa:Node2 .
</code></pre>
</section>
